From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windowscodecs: A HEIF decoder over libheif (6539)

HEIF images (HEIC: iPhone photos) decode through WIC on Windows once the
HEIF and HEVC extensions are installed; Wine had no HEIF decoder, so
FastStone, IrfanView's WIC path and the shell's thumbnails showed none.

windowscodecs now has a HEIF decoder (CLSID_WICHeifDecoder, the HEIF
container format, .heic/.heif/.hif, the ftyp brands of HEIF still
images). Its Unix side loads libheif at run time (libheif1 and its HEVC
plugin, libheif-plugin-libde265) and decodes the primary image, with its
rotation and mirroring applied, to 32-bit BGR(A). Without libheif or the
plugin the decoder declines and WIC finds no component for the file
(WINCODEC_ERR_COMPONENTNOTFOUND), as on Windows without the extensions.
wine.inf gives .heic, .heif and .hif the image thumbnail handler and an
image perceived type.
